{
 "name": "Iowa MIS Woodwinds (music-production build)",
 "comment": "Recorded by the University of Iowa Electronic Music Studios (Musical Instrument Samples, https://theremin.music.uiowa.edu/MIS.html) in an anechoic chamber, 5 feet from the instrument; the site states that since 1997 the recordings \"may be downloaded and used for any projects, without restrictions.\" Bass clarinet (Christine Bellomy, 1998), E-flat clarinet, alto flute and bass flute, chromatic at pp, mf and ff, mono, 16-bit/44.1 kHz, without vibrato. Bass clarinet on program 70, E-flat clarinet on 71, alto flute on 73, bass flute on 74; sustain on bank 0, one preset per recorded dynamic on banks 16-18 and legato presets on banks 32-34. Each note loops on its steady part. Each source file, a chromatic run at one dynamic, is cut into one note per file and every note checked against the run its file is named for (soundbank.py split); then pitch-checked again, intonation offsets within a semitone corrected by fineTune, leading silence trimmed, levels matched per layer with set layer offsets, 16-bit TPDF dither. In build b2 the steady hiss and rumble of every take are reduced by up to 12 dB: a Wiener gain against the noise measured in the quiet frames of each dynamic's takes.",
 "copyright": "Source recordings: University of Iowa Electronic Music Studios, free for any use without restrictions",
